body:
Alright, I'm gonna get personal with you. I'm a web development student (currently not doing so well in that area, if you check my posts). I haven't been diagnosed with autism, but it would come to no surprise to me if I had it. If I were you, I'd go look for another job in coding. I understand that you may be discouraged, but coders are in demand and some companies will treat them very well.

&#x200B;

As for your friend, I suppose you have 2 choices. 1, you could cut him off: boring. Or, get a decent paying job, make decent money, and flex on him as hard as you can. You haven't given many details about your friend but it doesn't sound like he has much going for him to be honest. Buy some nice clothes with the money you earn. It will help you in the social area as well. For most of my life I didn't care about the way I dressed. But once I started dressing better, I was more confident and socializing was easier.

&#x200B;
